he direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($⌣$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($⌢$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nWe can see that the function is curved upwards like a smile ($⌣$) over the intervals $(-3,-1)$ and $(1,3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041640/assets/ae9ce6ca2597a4d5d1ca150c1e97d7c7a0a35f59fe5d6421b75203c6882d2052.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51432/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51c15d7a-cd9c-58df-a750-97df0b695c64"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113899/selection/b31e00782a0d8a0a414a995cae2c860a700ece0e30725f0981808172c3bd79f8" :answer/id #uuid "06c683a2-2d0e-5c01-9e87-86a4e05dae88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113899/selection/917747ed806fd495b0bd48fa7c96466a148cf287f98ed26a585cb1c448274432" :answer/id #uuid "ba85e739-dd4f-52a8-85f9-ba7ec51f974c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113899/selection/f7a3c3073fd18240f3ef35ac5cf3afc829874542a015d352c8124afbc192acb3" :answer/id #uuid "9b1e8526-0a84-5038-aa10-071bae65c8d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113899/selection/93b236c9f6390974519135b3a74a68a187221ca65303f87151813c65429520b6" :answer/id #uuid "065ca941-e234-5a92-b802-2932bbf44834" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113899/selection/3e72be51e460f63fb53d45bcdf386a238f4fbffdd5f4e90828eb20f5d4414e2c" :answer/id #uuid "2a58dad1-934e-5a45-915a-76e3b2021887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "